course: dictionary
lesson: 14928
title: Getting something back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To regain something means to get it back after you have lost it. «After the wobble on the bike, Sam quickly regained his balance.» Sam lost his balance, then he got it back, so regained means got back.
explain: Look for the clue hidden in the word. The start, re-, often means again, and the rest, gain, means to get or win something. Put them together and you get: to win something again.
explain: The word can also mean reaching a place again, which is a more formal use. «After a stormy voyage, the sailors finally regained the shore.» They had been away at sea, and now they were back on land. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «they got back to the shore» still make sense? Yes, so you are right.
fact: Regain means to get back something you have lost.
fact: Regain is a verb: regain, regains, regained, regaining.
fact: Common phrases include regain control, regain consciousness, regain your balance and regain the lead.
fact: «Regained» is the past tense: «She regained her balance on the wet rocks.»
fact: In formal writing, regain can mean to reach a place again: «They regained the shore.»
exercise: «After the wobble on the bike, Sam quickly regained his balance.» What did Sam get back? | A spare helmet | *His balance | A lost shoe | A new bike
exercise: «The team fell behind, but in the last minute they regained the lead.» What does regained the lead mean? | They stopped playing | *They got back to being in front | They swapped their kit | They lost the game
exercise: Which word means to get something back after losing it? | forget | hide | sink | *regain
test: «The nurse said the patient had regained consciousness.» What does regained consciousness mean? | The patient lost their glasses | The patient fell asleep for the night | The patient left the hospital | *The patient woke up and became aware again
test: «After the long swim, the tired girl finally regained the side of the pool.» Which word fits best in the gap: The lost sailors at last ___ the shore. | forgot | hid | *regained | dropped
exam: «After the storm, the captain slowly regained control of the ship.» What does regained control mean? | *She got back the ability to steer it | She sold the ship | She painted the ship | She lost the ship forever
